 ## Overview
-Block Face Mesh Generation generates a 6-vertex mesh data structure for a single exposed face of a voxel block, applying special geometric adjustments for specific block types (such as cactus) and packing vertex attributes for GPU consumption [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [Face Direction and Quad Geometry](4881-face-direction-and-quad-geometry.md) by handling block-specific geometry modifications (like cactus insets) and attribute packing, rather than just providing generic face normals and UVs. It serves as the concrete implementation step within [Voxel Face Mesh Generation](4212-voxel-face-mesh-generation.md) that populates the `MeshData` buffer with the final vertex and index data for a specific block instance.
+Block Face Mesh Generation generates vertex and index data for a single exposed face of a voxel block, applying block-specific geometric adjustments and packing vertex attributes for GPU consumption [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [Face Direction and Quad Geometry](4881-face-direction-and-quad-geometry.md) by handling block-specific geometry modifications (like cactus insets) and attribute packing, rather than just providing generic face normals and UVs [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It serves as the concrete implementation step within [Voxel Face Mesh Generation](4212-voxel-face-mesh-generation.md) that populates the mesh buffer with the final vertex and index data for a specific block instance [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
